{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":31587,"duration_api_ms":31557,"num_turns":6,"result":"","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"13eae6f0-d9a1-4bb6-85fe-a41e045158d3","total_cost_usd":0.22829424999999998,"usage":{"input_tokens":5,"cache_creation_input_tokens":22409,"cache_read_input_tokens":106976,"output_tokens":1389,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":22409,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":5,"outputTokens":1389,"cacheReadInputTokens":106976,"cacheCreationInputTokens":22409,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.22829424999999998,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"summary":"Both amendments identify genuine test quality defects confirmed by reading the source. The first test is provably tautological (multiply then divide by the same volume_l recovers the original concentration by arithmetic identity, never exercising production code). The second test's assertion was weakened to only check a generic prefix string, missing the parameter name, value, and range that constitute the actual diagnostic payload.","votes":[{"amendment_id":"fr-6-49d40a08","decision":"accept","rationale":"Confirmed tautological: line 982 `tan_c = tan_total / volume_l` is algebraically identical to `tan_conc` (line 976 sets `tan_total = tan_conc * volume_l`). The same identity holds for no2_c, doc_c, do_c. Every subsequent `monod(tan_c, K) - monod(tan_conc, K)` comparison is comparing a value to itself. No production function (step_nitrogen_cycle, B2 helpers, or any shared concentration helper) is ever invoked — only a local lambda and ProcessParams::default(). A regression that passes total mass instead of concentration to the actual nitrogen cycle would not be detected by this test. It should be replaced with a test that calls the real production path."},{"amendment_id":"fr-6-01ebb675","decision":"accept","rationale":"Confirmed weakened assertion: the test at line 316 deliberately sets aob_k_tan_mg_n_per_l = 200.0 against valid_range [0.1, 5.0] to trigger a diagnostic, but the assertions (lines 333-334) only verify diagnostics.len() == 1 and that the message contains the generic prefix 'warning: preset `test` in category `process`'. It never checks that the warning mentions `aob_k_tan_mg_n_per_l`, the out-of-range value 200.0, or the expected range [0.1, 5.0]. A bug that emits a warning about the wrong parameter name, wrong value, or wrong range would still pass. The assertion should be strengthened to validate the actual diagnostic content."}]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"acabd069-46f4-48cc-a73f-a983820c1f7a"}
